WEBVTT

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:04.210
For the future

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:42.650
Dad? Mom?

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:07.100
You mean there's another room in the ruins?

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.350
I can't really remember it clearly...

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.000
Are you serious?

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:13.330
I didn't see any room like that.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:18.690
That room is definitely in those ruins!

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.900
We just couldn't find it.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.530
Hey, let me go there again!

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:25.930
If I go, I'm sure I'll be able to find something out.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:31.100
You have a point. We only just found the environmental control room the last time we went.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:32.530
It's been bothering me all this time.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:35.110
"Why was Adam in those ruins?"

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:39.050
It would be consistent with the ruins being a space ship.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:41.940
It's true.

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:47.530
Guessin' from that machinery, there's a good possibility of it bein' a space ship.

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:51.160
Then...

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:54.130
...we might be able to get home?

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:58.700
Wait. Even if it is a space ship, that doesn't mean it works.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.350
That's not all.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.630
They had the technology to make such an elaborate terraforming machine...

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:10.180
...so it wouldn't be weird if there was a better communicator in the ruins than the one I fixed.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:12.280
It's worth taking a look.

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:16.330
But we can't just search like we have up until now.

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:18.760
We're prepared for that.

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:20.940
You plan to spend the night on the ruins?

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:25.030
I mean, we can't investigate it properly unless we spend a whole day.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:26.300
I'll go too.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:28.660
Luna...

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:32.980
I'd like to take Adam with us. We want to borrow Adam's power so we can get into the ruins.

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:36.730
Let me go, Luna.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:37.850
You're okay with it?

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:39.390
I want to go.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.880
I might find out something about myself.

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:43.930
Please.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.090
Adam...

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:53.490
Okay.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:58.660
Kaoru, can you take them to the ruins?

00:04:58.660 --> 00:04:59.260
Yeah.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:03.760
The rest of us will take shifts at looking after their food.

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:05.600
No choice, I guess.

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:21.910
Well, I'll be taking these three to the ruins.

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:22.960
We're counting on you.

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:24.130
See you later.

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:25.590
We'll be waiting for your delivery.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:27.760
Be careful, you three.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:29.860
Don't make that face, Luna.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:31.250
Don't worry.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:37.850
Right, should we go?

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:39.310
Toodle-oo.

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:41.600
Hey, be careful.

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:43.740
Thanks. See you later!

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:46.740
Let's get going too.

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:17.710
And it was piled so high before...

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:29.150
Hey, look!

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:32.490
Everyone's House!

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:34.740
We're finally back!

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:43.890
We're home.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:48.840
We're finally here.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:51.050
Let's search every nook and cranny.

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.180
Huh? Huh, huh?

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:03.180
It opened so easily.

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:06.800
Those weirdos from before were definitely interfering.

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:09.010
Yeah, yeah! It was their fault!

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:18.950
Luna!

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:21.650
Alduram Gyet.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:25.400
.ni yats ot uoy rof reisae eb lliw ereh tnemnorivne eht ,nooS

00:07:25.890 --> 00:07:28.440
What do you mean by an environment easier for Adam to stay in?

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:30.390
Adam spends every day shivering!

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:32.390
Luna!

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:37.180
Adam!

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:45.460
What are you doing? Adam's your child, isn't he?

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:57.460
See you.

00:07:57.650 --> 00:07:58.480
Kaoru...

00:07:58.700 --> 00:07:59.530
Thanks.

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:02.560
Say thanks to everyone for us too!

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:06.650
Alright... begin search!

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:17.000
--Bell, a little lower!
--Give me a second!

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:33.240
This is all there is after all?

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:36.390
We don't have any other information about it being a space ship.

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:40.480
No matter how much I look, I can't find anythin' new.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:47.830
Because we shut it down to stop the main energy field...

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:50.040
...we can't make it work well.

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:53.680
I can't find any systems other than terraforming, either.

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:58.550
Hey, Adam, whereabouts was the room you saw in your dream?

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:00.160
I can't...

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:02.340
...remember very clearly.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:05.680
Anything is fine, so do your best to remember.

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:06.880
Please!

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:42.200
Not here either?

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:08.560
Heavy...

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:10.700
Howard, nice work.

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:14.490
Now we have everything we're going to take to them tomorrow.

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:19.060
It's already been five days.

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.760
I've already checked there three times.

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:39.160
I know, but...

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:37.100
Alduram Gyet.

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:44.710
...fo erutuf eht roF

00:11:45.130 --> 00:11:46.780
Alduram Gyet.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:11.900
This is...

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:14.260
What kinda trick was that?

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:18.880
That's...

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:34.930
It's here!

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:02.150
Amazin'!

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:04.180
Let's go!

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:05.830
You bet!

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:18.910
It's the cockpit.

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:22.930
Chako, these ruins themselves were a spaceship!

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:24.200
They sure were!

00:13:41.790 --> 00:13:46.180
For Alduram Gyet's future.

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:49.890
For my future...

00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:53.710
There's lots of energy, too!

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:56.380
This space ship might move!

00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:58.380
Anyways, we have to check it all out!

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:02.230
This looks like the energy unit.

00:14:02.410 --> 00:14:04.700
Which means this is the reactor unit?

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:07.510
Looks like they're similar to earth's.

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:09.650
What about the communicator?

00:14:13.060 --> 00:14:14.260
Maybe it's this!

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:17.940
I should be able to figure it out in an hour.

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:20.230
It's all thanks to Adam!

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:35.940
This space ship was shot out of the main terraforming unit.

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:40.100
Then the space ship's mother ship is on the continent?

00:14:40.550 --> 00:14:41.560
Looks like it.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:56.830
It's receiving properly. The communicator's perfect!

00:14:58.330 --> 00:14:59.790
It's got plenty of energy, too.

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:03.240
Let's set it to transmit the distress signal constantly.

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:05.860
Since we've done so much, let's take a break first.

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:10.360
We're takin' a break, Adam.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:12.730
Thank you.

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:15.310
It's all because you were able to remember.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:22.700
Luna!

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:26.750
This is...

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:31.630
Then these ruins themselves are a space ship?

00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:33.540
There's no doubt about it.

00:15:34.210 --> 00:15:35.110
Does it work?

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:37.060
Well, that's the problem.

00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:39.460
It doesn't work for some reason.

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:42.050
But we can use the communicator, right?

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.510
Maybe we should call everyone here.

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:47.600
I'll go.

00:15:48.350 --> 00:15:49.590
Sorry to make you, but please do.

00:15:49.850 --> 00:15:51.500
We'll be back tomorrow by noon.

00:15:56.380 --> 00:15:57.240
Where's Adam?

00:15:58.780 --> 00:15:59.490
I dunno.

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:03.050
Adam ain't been cheerful at all since we found the cockpit.

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:04.480
That's true.

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:06.430
Really...

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:30.050
Dad...

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:31.960
Mom...

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:02.340
Are you okay?

00:17:09.050 --> 00:17:11.040
Adam! This is where you were?

00:17:12.200 --> 00:17:13.630
Thanks, Kaoru.

00:17:13.890 --> 00:17:14.750
No...

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:16.700
Be careful!

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:27.310
I see...

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:32.710
The people in your dreams were your father and mother after all.

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:38.340
I wonder how my mom and dad felt about me.

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:43.630
I'm sure you were very precious to them, Adam.

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:48.800
They left you with the words, "For Alduram Gyet's future," after all.

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:50.560
That must...

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:52.180
..be false!

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:53.410
Why?

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:56.260
They were mean to us, Luna.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:59.260
I'm sure that was just some sort of mistake.

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:06.580
I think their feelings of wanting to leave you a place that would be easy to stay in were real.

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:08.380
But they made it snow.

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:10.290
They must have hated me.

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:12.580
Because I was a burden to them.

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:15.990
Do you really think that?

00:18:17.790 --> 00:18:21.650
The mom and dad in my dream seemed so nice.

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:24.240
So why?

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:26.410
I'm sure they had a reason.

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:30.730
From what I saw of them, they seemed to be very kind.

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:33.730
I'm sure they didn't hate you at all!

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:35.980
They definitely didn't!

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:42.010
You have to believe in them. Okay?

00:18:46.590 --> 00:18:47.490
I guess so.

00:18:57.160 --> 00:18:58.740
Dad!

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:00.200
Mom!

00:19:01.060 --> 00:19:02.490
I miss you!

00:19:05.980 --> 00:19:06.950
Adam...

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:46.210
Ready.

00:19:53.560 --> 00:19:54.460
No good.

00:19:55.060 --> 00:19:56.600
That's weird...

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:58.600
There's plenty of energy.

00:19:58.850 --> 00:20:01.180
I can't see any faults in the electrical system either.

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:03.160
Why don't it work?

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:04.060
How is it?

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:09.050
At this rate, smoke'll start comin' outta my head.

00:20:10.630 --> 00:20:12.350
You seem in high spirits today, Adam.

00:20:12.760 --> 00:20:14.380
You were pretty depressed for a while.

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:16.660
He cheered up 'cuz Luna's here.

00:20:16.850 --> 00:20:18.050
Right, Adam?

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:19.590
So that's it.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:25.360
Since Adam's cheerful again, we'd better try once more!

00:20:25.930 --> 00:20:26.600
I guess so!

00:20:29.380 --> 00:20:30.430
What'dja push?

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:33.460
This is...

00:20:35.230 --> 00:20:36.690
A self-diagnostic program!

00:20:39.350 --> 00:20:40.810
What's that?

00:20:40.810 --> 00:20:42.460
That's what's broken.

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:45.350
This is probably the energy flow...

00:20:45.610 --> 00:20:48.010
The gyrostabilizer seems okay.

00:20:48.130 --> 00:20:51.280
Oh no! This is definitely the gravity control unit!

00:20:52.510 --> 00:20:53.300
Really?

00:20:53.530 --> 00:20:54.650
Can you fix it?

00:20:55.060 --> 00:20:56.750
It'd be impossible for us right now.

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:59.260
Without a gravity control unit, we're stopped dead.

00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:01.510
Even though we tried so hard!

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:03.350
Then the space ship...

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:07.480
Well, it can't be helped.

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:10.550
Isn't it good enough that we can use the communicator?

00:21:11.190 --> 00:21:12.690
That may be true...

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:15.050
That's it!

00:21:15.240 --> 00:21:17.560
The reason the gravity in the Eastern Woods was weird...

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:20.940
...was 'cuz the gravity control unit of this space ship was broken!

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:22.780
Yeah... but...

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:27.350
Let's take a little break.

00:21:31.550 --> 00:21:32.410
Luna!

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:37.550
Sharla... everyone!

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:39.760
So these ruins were a space ship?

00:21:40.140 --> 00:21:41.230
When can we get going?

00:21:41.530 --> 00:21:42.650
Let's go home soon!

00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:44.650
Stop talkin' about that right now.

00:21:44.650 --> 00:21:47.830
Don't act so important! Shingo, how about it?

00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:50.530
What's wrong?

00:21:51.130 --> 00:21:55.250
We found out that the gravity control unit is broken, so it won't run.

00:21:56.150 --> 00:21:57.650
What's up with that?

00:21:57.800 --> 00:21:59.940
Then there was no point in us coming all this way!

00:22:00.090 --> 00:22:01.210
That's not true!

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:04.700
We found out that the communicator still works perfectly.

00:22:04.700 --> 00:22:07.030
What's so good about having a communicator?

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:09.500
We don't know when help will come.

00:22:09.840 --> 00:22:11.410
We got our hopes up for nothing.

00:22:11.900 --> 00:22:14.560
Luna, is that the cockpit?

00:22:23.860 --> 00:22:25.810
So there was a room like this.

00:22:32.150 --> 00:22:33.240
What is it?

00:22:36.610 --> 00:22:37.890
Is it over?

00:22:45.650 --> 00:22:47.860
This is the Orion. [garbled]

00:22:48.310 --> 00:22:50.680
This is [garbled]. Please respond.

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:53.150
Distress signal received.

00:22:54.010 --> 00:22:57.730
This is the Orion. We've received your distress signal.

00:23:03.730 --> 00:23:06.160
Alright! We connected with the radio!

00:23:06.160 --> 00:23:10.290
Ain't it great? Shingo's finally been paid back for his trouble!

00:23:10.510 --> 00:23:12.280
Hurry up and save us!

00:23:12.280 --> 00:23:14.600
Rescue ship, thanks.

00:23:14.940 --> 00:23:17.230
But it seems strange.

00:23:17.860 --> 00:23:20.600
It's true. The radio cut out in the middle.

00:23:21.350 --> 00:23:24.200
Anyways, we have to tell them the location of this island.

00:23:25.590 --> 00:23:28.290
Next time: Do you read me?
